      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, did you just say \"exceeding the initial target by 300%\"? We didn't actually exceed the target, the target was 20% and we only got 5%. If they audit our internal reports and see that we're claiming we smashed our targets when we actually missed them by a mile, we'll be blacklisted from all future funding. \n\nBut at the same time, if we just tell them the truth—that we failed to hit our mark—we lose the grant. Is there a way to write it so it sounds like a massive success without using numbers that are technically impossible to defend if they audit us? Like, can we just make it sound like the 5% is actually a huge deal without explicitly lying about the 20% goal?",
